{
  "esm": "1.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "Relational",
    "description": "Standard-library relational templates (esm-spec §9.7.1 template-library file). Two match-less expression templates give the pure-AST definitions of the `argmin` and `argmax` arg-witness reducers: `argmin(f, n)` and `argmax(f, n)`, the 1-based index in [1, n] of the smallest (largest) candidate value `f`, where `f` is an expression over the template's loop symbol (`k_argmin_1`, `k_argmax_1`) and n, the number of candidates, is an explicit integer parameter. Ties go to the smallest index and a NaN candidate wins at its first occurrence. Written with two `faq` reductions, `ifelse` and comparisons only. Import with `expression_template_imports` and invoke with `apply_expression_template`; see docs/content/standard_library.md.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML"
    ],
    "created": "2026-11-07T00:00:00Z",
    "tags": [
      "standard-library",
      "relational",
      "argmin",
      "argmax",
      "arg-witness",
      "expression-templates"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "esm-spec.md §4.2 (argmin, argmax; NaN in min/max reductions); §9.6 (expression templates); §9.7.1 (template-library files); RFC semiring-faq-unified-ir §5.7 rule 6 (smallest-index tie-break)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "argmin": {
      "params": [
        "f",
        "n"
      ],
      "description": "1-based index k in [1, n] at which the candidate value `f` attains its minimum. `f` is an expression over the loop symbol `k_argmin_1`, which this template binds to each candidate index in turn (write the candidate's value with `k_argmin_1` as its index, e.g. `index(d, i, k_argmin_1)`). Two `faq` reductions: m = min over k_argmin_1 of f, then the smallest k_argmin_1 at which f == m. On a tie the smallest index wins (RFC semiring-faq-unified-ir §5.7 rule 6). If any candidate is NaN, m is NaN (esm-spec §4.2) and the result is the index of the first NaN candidate. n = 0 gives +Inf (the identity of the `min` reduction). `f` is written twice in the expansion; it must not itself bind `k_argmin_1` for another purpose.",
      "body": {
        "op": "faq",
        "args": [],
        "output_idx": [],
        "reduce": "min",
        "ranges": {
          "k_argmin_1": [
            1,
            "n"
          ]
        },
        "expr": {
          "op": "ifelse",
          "args": [
            {
              "op": "or",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "==",
                  "args": [
                    "f",
                    {
                      "op": "faq",
                      "args": [],
                      "output_idx": [],
                      "reduce": "min",
                      "ranges": {
                        "k_argmin_1": [
                          1,
                          "n"
                        ]
                      },
                      "expr": "f"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "and",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "!=",
                      "args": [
                        "f",
                        "f"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "!=",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "faq",
                          "args": [],
                          "output_idx": [],
                          "reduce": "min",
                          "ranges": {
                            "k_argmin_1": [
                              1,
                              "n"
                            ]
                          },
                          "expr": "f"
                        },
                        {
                          "op": "faq",
                          "args": [],
                          "output_idx": [],
                          "reduce": "min",
                          "ranges": {
                            "k_argmin_1": [
                              1,
                              "n"
                            ]
                          },
                          "expr": "f"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "k_argmin_1",
            {
              "op": "+",
              "args": [
                "n",
                1
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "argmax": {
      "params": [
        "f",
        "n"
      ],
      "description": "1-based index k in [1, n] at which the candidate value `f` attains its maximum. `f` is an expression over the loop symbol `k_argmax_1`, which this template binds to each candidate index in turn (write the candidate's value with `k_argmax_1` as its index, e.g. `index(d, i, k_argmax_1)`). Two `faq` reductions: m = max over k_argmax_1 of f, then the smallest k_argmax_1 at which f == m. On a tie the smallest index wins (RFC semiring-faq-unified-ir §5.7 rule 6). If any candidate is NaN, m is NaN (esm-spec §4.2) and the result is the index of the first NaN candidate. n = 0 gives +Inf (the identity of the `min` reduction). `f` is written twice in the expansion; it must not itself bind `k_argmax_1` for another purpose.",
      "body": {
        "op": "faq",
        "args": [],
        "output_idx": [],
        "reduce": "min",
        "ranges": {
          "k_argmax_1": [
            1,
            "n"
          ]
        },
        "expr": {
          "op": "ifelse",
          "args": [
            {
              "op": "or",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "==",
                  "args": [
                    "f",
                    {
                      "op": "faq",
                      "args": [],
                      "output_idx": [],
                      "reduce": "max",
                      "ranges": {
                        "k_argmax_1": [
                          1,
                          "n"
                        ]
                      },
                      "expr": "f"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "and",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "!=",
                      "args": [
                        "f",
                        "f"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "!=",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "faq",
                          "args": [],
                          "output_idx": [],
                          "reduce": "max",
                          "ranges": {
                            "k_argmax_1": [
                              1,
                              "n"
                            ]
                          },
                          "expr": "f"
                        },
                        {
                          "op": "faq",
                          "args": [],
                          "output_idx": [],
                          "reduce": "max",
                          "ranges": {
                            "k_argmax_1": [
                              1,
                              "n"
                            ]
                          },
                          "expr": "f"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "k_argmax_1",
            {
              "op": "+",
              "args": [
                "n",
                1
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
